CORE
main.c
--generate-function-body '(?!__CPROVER).*' --generate-function-body-options assume-false
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
may interfere with analysis
--
This replaces the removed option --undefined-function-is-assume-false: each
function without a body is given the body assume(false).  The removed option
rewrote each call of such a function instead, and produced a goto binary that
could not be read back when a call was the target of a jump, as are the calls
in the branches of the if and the calls created for the function pointer.
